3. UGC STEP IN THE CLOSEOUT RING (measured, refused by a shipped law, NOT landed)
   Board head R3390 item (1) asked for ("ugc", "tools/ugc_gate_report.py", [])
   in tools/closeout_order.py STEPS. Measured three times:
   (a) ugc after backhop: ring PASS3 reads face_sweep 12/13 with entry-index
       21/23; deliverable_index --check prints
       FAIL AC-DIX21 reason='no producer is recorded for ugc-gate-report.json'
       FAIL AC-DIX23 pair=ugc-gate-report.json producer=- one-command-or-absence=False
   (b) recording the producer in PAIR_PRODUCERS, then --
       FAIL AC-DIX21 mode=check cmd='python tools/ugc_gate_report.py --check'
       html=28799B json=20170B rc=0 html-eq-row=False printed-once=False
       because the bare render is 28112B while the landed page is 28799B.
   (c) reordering ugc BEFORE backhop so the ring injects the channel itself:
       ring still ends on the same AC-DIX21/AC-DIX23 pair (index 21/23).
   Root cause measured, not guessed: tools/ugc_gate_report.py writes a document
   with no back-hop block and tools/face_backhop.py injects it afterwards, so the
   pair has TWO writers and no single recorded command reproduces the on-disk
   bytes the entry page quotes. The index one-command law therefore refuses it.
   The step was reverted; the measurement is recorded as the next-window item.

